alias ExitStatus = std::process::ExitStatus;
alias Inputs = std::process::Inputs;

public fn run(inputs: Inputs) -> status: ExitStatus pure waits doc "The layout_oracle entry, invoked as `layout_oracle MODE REPS PAGE UA [SUFFIX=SHEET ...]` with the style oracle's arguments, from the repository root, with the installed fonts copied into build/fonts. It loads the page and its sheets with pkg::oracle::page, computes styles and loads the fonts, then: dump matches the fonts, builds and lays out the page once and writes the format of tests/layout/layout_oracle.mjs to standard output; boxes, text and layout repeat REPS times the stage's parts in nested order, so that the time of each part is the difference between consecutive modes: boxes builds the box tree, text also matches each font group's faces (pkg::layout::text::pick_fonts) and prepares every paragraph's text (font matching, shaping and break opportunities), and layout also lays the tree out; each prints the mode, the element, context and paragraph counts and REPS. nodes (REPS 0) lists the nodes of the document in tree order, without styles or fonts: an element as `E NODE DEPTH NAME DESCENDANTS INDEX` (NODE the node identifier, DEPTH the number of element ancestors, DESCENDANTS the number of elements below it, INDEX its position in the traversal), a Text node as `T NODE PARENT LENGTH DATA` (LENGTH in bytes, DATA with backslash written `\\` and line feed `\n`), and last `N COUNT`, the number of nodes the document holds. edit takes the path of an edit script in place of REPS: it loads the page, applies the script's S lines, runs the whole pipeline (traversal, styles, font matching, layout, placement) on the live document and prints `base hash H bytes N`, H being the FNV-1a 64-bit hash of the dump in 16 hexadecimal digits and N its size; then, for each edit line in order, it applies the edit to the live document, reruns the pipeline and prints `edit I hash H bytes N` (I from 1); after a T/D text edit, C/K style edit or B/X child-list edit, which it also applies to a layout kept across edits with pkg::layout's text_changed, styles_changed or consuming children_changed followed by update, the line ends in ` inc same` or ` inc DIFF` as the kept layout's dump is or is not byte for byte the rebuilt one's, or ` inc refused` when text_changed, styles_changed, children_changed or update refused the edit (a P line's dump of a differing edit is followed by the line `inc dump` and the incremental dump), and the kept layout becomes the rebuilt one after a difference, a refusal or any other edit. Checking also reports style-update work as `style edit I prepared R contexts C paragraphs P held_entries H entries E`. incremental takes the script as edit does, applies each T/D text edit, C/K style edit and B/X child-list edit to the kept layout and prints `edit I us U prepared R contexts C paragraphs P held_entries H entries E`, U the microseconds of text_changed and update for text edits, or layout_changes, font picking, styles_changed and update for style edits, or layout_changes, font picking, children_changed and update for child-list edits, and the rest pkg::layout's update_counts, or `edit I inc refused` after rebuilding the layout, and rebuilds it after any other edit, printing `edit I full`. Traversal and style recomputation stay outside the timed layout interval; a separate `style edit I delta_us D picks_us P full_us F` line gives the delta and font-picking portions and a full comparator using fresh font picks, build_layout and lay_out on the same edited document and computed styles, excluding style computation and placement. The script has one operation per line: `S CSS` adds the rest of the line as an author style sheet after the page's own, only before the first edit; `T NODE OFFSET TEXT` inserts the rest of the line (with `\\` and `\n` resolved) into a Text node's data at a byte offset; `D NODE OFFSET LENGTH` deletes bytes of a Text node's data; `C ELEMENT TOKEN` and `K ELEMENT TOKEN` add a token to and remove a token from an element's class attribute; `B PARENT BEFORE TEXT` inserts a new HTML p element holding one Text node of the text into PARENT before the node BEFORE (`-` for the end) and prints `created NODE` before the edit's line; `X NODE` detaches a node; `P I` requests the full dump of edit I (0 for the unedited document) after its hash line. The style attributes and presentational hints are recorded once, at load, by stable NodeId, so adding or removing an element does not move their ownership. Child-list updates record the old parent before X and the fresh child identity before B; they emit a separate child edit line with the same work-count fields in checking mode, and delta_us, picks_us and full_us in timing mode. After each successful child-list update, both modes also emit exactly one `child work I sources_built B sources_retained R paragraphs_reused P text_routes_written TW source_routes_written SW text_routes_changed TC source_routes_changed SC old_route_capacity O route_capacity C route_slots_copied M` line outside the timed interval, using child_update_counts from the retained result. This line is absent on refusal, and is separate from the existing child edit geometry counts or timings. A refusal is reported explicitly even if the driver rebuilds to continue the script. Exits 2 when the invocation, a file, the page, the style stage, the layout stage or an edit script line fails.";
